-- Showcase Level 3 (design sum-type-showcase): userspace `observe` with a
-- continuous base and an inequality predicate -- a truncated Normal. The kept
-- arm is a dim-1 density restricted to the positive half-line; the rejected arm
-- is the dim-0 mass of the complement, measured through the CDF by the
-- set-valued witness machinery (design set-valued-witnesses).
--
-- `p(Right ANY)` (= P(Just ANY) = 0.5) is the denominator of the
-- renormalization identity: dividing the kept arm by it turns the restricted
-- density into a proper truncated Normal, `2*phi(v)*1[v>0]`. Structural MAR
-- inside a constructor slot of a continuous comparison target used to crash
-- here (observe-partials-umbrella's "known adjacent gap"); it is answered by
-- the set-witness engine's runtime point-or-interval choice, task
-- set-witness-any-in-constructor-slot.
main = let v = Normal in if v > 0.0 then right v else left ()
